WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.635
lip-dictation lets

00:00:01.447 --> 00:00:02.413
you mouth prompts

00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.144
to Claude Code

00:00:03.678 --> 00:00:04.656
A Claude Code

00:00:04.468 --> 00:00:05.517
plugin that reads

00:00:05.329 --> 00:00:06.095
your lips through

00:00:05.907 --> 00:00:06.755
the webcam with

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:08.336
the Auto-AVSR model

00:00:08.159 --> 00:00:09.361
running locally on

00:00:09.173 --> 00:00:10.128
Apple Silicon

00:00:10.341 --> 00:00:10.942
so you can

00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:12.192
send prompts silently

00:00:12.718 --> 00:00:13.519
Press a button

00:00:13.331 --> 00:00:14.215
above the Claude

00:00:14.027 --> 00:00:14.864
Code prompt

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:15.960
mouth a phrase

00:00:16.043 --> 00:00:17.128
press stop and

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.012
the text appears

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:18.567
in the prompt

00:00:18.378 --> 00:00:19.545
box about half

00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:20.394
a second later

00:00:20.918 --> 00:00:23.276
Recognition uses Auto-AVSR's

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:28.005
visual-only model vsrtrlrs2lrs3vox2avspbase

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:29.703
250M parameters

00:00:29.798 --> 00:00:32.958
trained on 3,291 hours

00:00:32.769 --> 00:00:33.500
of video

00:00:33.639 --> 00:00:35.950
¹ Auto-AVSR model

00:00:35.762 --> 00:00:36.221
zoo

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:38.415
20.3% word error

00:00:38.227 --> 00:00:39.912
rate on LRS3

00:00:40.446 --> 00:00:41.460
Full story on

00:00:41.271 --> 00:00:42.167
the dashboard
